ip_or_cidr,version,community,v3_user,v3_level,v3_auth_proto,v3_auth_pass,v3_priv_proto,v3_priv_pass
# Copy to snmp_credentials.csv and fill in as you onboard devices/subnets.
# Rows are optional and incremental -- an IP with no matching row here just
# stays resolved via syslog's own hostname field (or unresolved), it does
# not block anything else in the pipeline.
#
# Single device, SNMPv2c:
# 10.10.1.5,v2c,my-ro-community,,,,,,
#
# Whole subnet sharing one v2c community:
# 10.10.2.0/24,v2c,another-community,,,,,,
#
# Single device, SNMPv3:
# 10.10.3.10,v3,,readonly_user,authPriv,SHA,authpassword123,AES,privpassword123
